			<div class="content" id="post-content-4818379">
									

<p>What if the legends of heroes, their birth, and their exploits we all have come to known had a more ulterior motive? An ulterior motive from a third party?</p>
<p><em>I moved and trimmed your thread summary, since it was taking up extra space in the main forum screen. Try to keep thread descriptions (the text in the little box under the thread title) and titles short so you don't crowd out other authors in the forum listing. ~Zyn</em></p>
<p>Seeking Greenlights: Yes</p>
<p>Page Type: SCP Article</p>
<p>Genre (Optional):</p>
<p>Page Layout (Optional): Standard SCP Article</p>
<p>Elevator Pitch: A rather gelatinous, clay-like sentient entity found in a rather sedated state found within the confines of the Great Ziggurat of Ur. It's capable of morphing into various shapes and sizes but will always have Sumerian Cuneiform markings on it's form and is capable of changing any terrestrial properties into an unknown metal. It is capable of speech but will morph its body into various holes and folds to create sound akin to speaking. Will often appear in either a bipedal humanoid form or a quadrupedal form with it's front two legs being longer and larger than its hind legs. It's body is 90% composed of clay with the other 10% percent being composed of an unknown metal that varies in magnetic properties, the very same type of metal he can create.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Narrative: Following reports from locals and tourists hearing sounds and voices being heard and sights of various metallic objects floating deep within the tourist wonder spot of Iraq known as the Great Ziggurat of Ur, MTF forces were soon sent in to investigate the anomalous nature of the event. What they found at first was a formless gelatinous, clay-like entity surrounded by various metallic spheres floating around it. It was found nestled in the pinnacle of the ziggurat where various humming from the spheres could be heard. What was more interesting was the fact that the entity was somehow turning the earth around it into some sort of metal, the same type of metal the spheres surrounding it was composed of. The article will provide a more in-depth explanation and briefing regarding first contact, anomalous properties, and interview regarding the SCP.</p>
<p>Hook/Attention-grabber: The entity is among many that is regarded as a failed experiment created by an unknown race of entities. It shares some sort of connection with SCP 4046 and SCP 073. At the mention of SCP 4044, the entity would release sounds akin to cooing with it's body vibrating. As though it was excited. With the first meeting with SCP 073, SCP personal would find themselves surprised of a rather violent reaction not from the entity but from SCP 073. A violent bout does take place, with SCP 073 referring the entity as a &quot;Faker&quot; and an &quot;insult to his brother&quot;. Further details of both events will be explained in more detail in the article.</p>
</div>
</div>
