<p><strong>Summoned via PM:</strong></p>
<p>Hi there ProfAurelius. Let’s take a look at your concept.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>What if the legends of heroes, their birth, and their exploits we all have come to known had a more ulterior motive? An ulterior motive from a third party?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Okay, you’ve got my attention. But this hook is also raising lots of red flags in terms of its scope and ambition for a first-timer piece.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The article will provide a more in-depth explanation and briefing regarding first contact, anomalous properties, and interview regarding the SCP.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>For those of us not familiar with SCP-4046, SCP-073 or Sumerian mythology, please would you kindly make the connection for us here? You’ve set up an intriguing shapeshifting and alchemy-capable entity without explaining what the connection is to your original pitch above. Who/what is the entity, what is it doing, why is it dangerous and how does it birth the “legends of heroes”?</p>
<p>If you decide to revise the concept / respond below, do drop me another PM and I’ll try my best to take a second look. For now, all the best!</p>

